-- Singapore Penal Code 1871 - documents-defamation group (Chapters 18, 20,
-- 21, 22; ss 463-510): what the group's parts share, and nothing that is a
-- rule of any one section.
--
-- Two builders for the two punishment shapes that almost every punishing
-- section in these Chapters uses. Each still takes the section's own words,
-- verbatim, and its maximum term; they only save repeating the fifteen fields
-- of `Punishment` (pc-general.l4) thirty times. A section whose punishment has
-- neither shape (s 507, s 474) spells its `Punishment` out in full.
--
--   "imprisonment for a term which may extend to N years, or with fine, or
--    with both"                     - `a punishment of imprisonment, or fine, or both`
--   "imprisonment for a term which may extend to N years, and shall also be
--    liable to fine"                - `a punishment of imprisonment, and liability to fine`
--
-- Source: Penal Code 1871, 2020 Revised Edition, SSO "Current version as at
-- 09 Sep 2026" (inputs/PC1871.txt).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pc-domain`
IMPORT `pc-general`

§ `documents-defamation - shared punishment shapes`

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 53, 465, 500-506 and the other sections in Chapters 18, 21 and 22 that say "... or with fine, or with both"
GIVEN section IS A STRING @desc The punishing section, as the Code prints it - for example "465"
      words   IS A STRING @desc The punishment in the section's own words, verbatim
      months  IS A NUMBER @desc The term the imprisonment "may extend to", in months
GIVETH A Punishment
`a punishment of imprisonment, or fine, or both` section words months MEANS
    Punishment WITH
        section                  IS section
        words                    IS words
        death                    IS `not prescribed`
        `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
        imprisonment             IS `or with`
        `maximum term in months` IS JUST months
        `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
        `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
        fine                     IS `or with`
        `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
        `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
        caning                   IS `not prescribed`
        `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
        `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
        `or with both`           IS TRUE

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 53, 466-468 and the other sections in Chapter 18 that say "... and shall also be liable to fine"
GIVEN section IS A STRING @desc The punishing section, as the Code prints it - for example "468"
      words   IS A STRING @desc The punishment in the section's own words, verbatim
      months  IS A NUMBER @desc The term the imprisonment "may extend to", in months
GIVETH A Punishment
`a punishment of imprisonment, and liability to fine` section words months MEANS
    Punishment WITH
        section                  IS section
        words                    IS words
        death                    IS `not prescribed`
        `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
        imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
        `maximum term in months` IS JUST months
        `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
        `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
        fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
        `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
        `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
        caning                   IS `not prescribed`
        `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
        `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
        `or with both`           IS FALSE
